protesters run for their lives a number  of people were killed here in this pnom  Penn suburb as government troops opened  fire in an effort to break up labor  protests many were wounded in the  crackdown the soldiers should be  protecting the sovereignty of the  country so I am wondering why they are  protecting this factory instead more  than half of the country's estimated  650,000 garment workers have gone on  strike many work for popular Western  brands like added ass Nike or H&amp;M  conditions at the factories here maybe  better than in Bangladesh but wages are  low just around 60 euros a month barely  enough to put food on the table workers  are demanding double that rate but the  government led by Prime Minister Hun Sen  has only offered a 25 percent increase  but the strikes pose a threat to Hun  Sen's nearly three decades rule the  garment industry is Cambodia's biggest  export earner and the protests are some  of the largest Cambodia has ever seen  the protesters are also backed by the  opposition they accuse Hansen of rigging  last year's vote and are calling on him  to step down they say
 

